{"type":"text","text":"Done. Sheet 1 for Super Mario Bros., scene World 1-1.\n\n**Where I started:** the emulator was already in game mode 1 (`$0770`=1) playing World 1-1, so no Start sequence was needed.\n\n**Small Mario (metasprite, `record_mapping` → sprite `small_mario`)**\n`list_sprites` over the whole frame returned 8 OAM entries in a 2-wide × 4-tall box (top-left at screen 40,177), all sprite **palette 4**; only the lower two rows are real, the top two rows are transparent `$FC` padding.\n\n| OAM | tile | offset | flip | role |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1–4 | `$FC` | (0,0) (8,0) (0,8) (8,8) | none | blank padding |\n| 5 | `$3A` | (0,16) | none | head left (hat/hair/face) |\n| 6 | `$37` | (8,16) | none | head right |\n| 7 | `$4F` | (0,24) | none | body left |\n| 8 | `$4F` | (8,24) | **h-flipped** | body right |\n\nProof: hit-tested at Mario pixel (44,204) → exactly OAM#7, `chr_tile` 79 (`$4F`), palette 4, no flip, opaque.\n\n**His colors (palette 4, `record_mapping` → palette `4`)**\n`get_palette 4` = `$22, $16, $27, $18`. I wrote slot 1 `$16` red → `$2C` cyan (frozen), stepped 1 frame and screenshotted: the cap and shirt/overalls turned cyan — `get_pixel_color` (48,193) and (45,193) = `$2C` — while the face (50,195) stayed `$27` orange and the hair/eye (49,195) stayed `$18` olive. So: slot 0 `$22` never paints (index 0 is transparent on sprites), slot 1 `$16` = cap + shirt/overalls, slot 2 `$27` = face/skin + hands, slot 3 `$18` = hair, outline, shoes. `clear_palette_overrides` restored `$16`.\n\n**Brick block (`record_mapping` → tiles `0x145`, `0x147`, group `brick`)**\nAfter holding Right (x 40→235) the floating brick row was on screen. `get_region` object mode at (232,152): 256 connected background palette-1 pixels, box (231,144)–(246,159), CHR `$145`/`$147`. Probing quadrants plus raw nametable (`$2650`=`45 45`, `$2670`=`47 47`) showed the 16×16 metatile is:\n\n- `$145` / CHR `$145` — **brick top-left** (also the top-right; the texture is designed to repeat horizontally)\n- `$147` / CHR `$147` — **brick bottom-left** (also the bottom-right; same texture minus the top highlight row)\n\nPalette 1 = `$36` peach highlight, `$17` brown face, `$0F` black mortar. These are distinct from the ground/floor bricks (`$B4`–`$B7`), which were already mapped under group `ground`.\n\n`promote_mappings` promoted all 4 (now 31 tiles, 8 palettes, 2 sprites, 26 addresses in the shared file). The emulator is left **paused** on the frame I verified."}
